id: pm-review-sdk-import-history-gap
title: Track core imported relationship history replay refusal
description: "Pinned core SDK 2026.10.20 reproduction on a plain tracker: create a source Task, create a target Task with a related dependency, verify historical version 1, readLocatedItem, change only description, and call commitImportedItem with that document. get at version 2 then refuses with history_replay_invalid and verify_failed:before_hash_mismatch:entry_2. This is outside revision-scoped review implementation; review scope safely returns history_unavailable instead of trusting the artifact. No source tracker history was repaired or rewritten."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-25T06:04:42.850Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-26T00:49:38.343Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Reproduce against current core SDK; Preserve existing native relationship fields and append-only replay integrity across imported updates; Keep review history refusals conservative until the upstream import path is fixed
parent: pm-review-epic
comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-25T06:06:39.645Z",codex-agent,"Confirmed independently with a minimal real non-git tracker on pinned SDK 2026.10.20: the only imported change was description on an existing Task with one related dependency. Historical version 1 read succeeded before import; version 2 read failed afterward with history_replay_invalid / verify_failed:before_hash_mismatch:entry_2. New-item SDK imports used for model seeding remain replayable. No workaround repairs or rewrites history. Report this SDK gap in the handoff; do not file upstream from this task."
  "2026-10-26T00:49:38.343Z",codex-agent,"Targeted evidence validation reproduced the existing core import-history limitation with the pinned 2026.10.20 SDK: importing a rich native document over an existing linked-artifact item reported verify_failed:before_hash_mismatch:entry_2, and historical get refused history_replay_invalid. The new read-only request queue rejects that evidence as evidence_unavailable and never repairs its history. Its model seeds a fresh native document, uses SDK mutations, and replays its own packet/arrival inputs; no native import/export/sync writer is added."
